# FABLE-SONNET-OWN-LOOKUP-AUDIT-20260923-131 Part 2 (b): re-verifying
# l2_check_sizeof's l2_own_find_last call (fired only when l2_own_find
# already failed) against -129's fallback. `x` is a unit field, read via
# `sizeof:` from inside a nested method -- backward-visible per the
# author's norm, same as any other read. Since -129 gave l2_own_find_last
# the same unit-fallback l2_own_find already had, this call site's second
# try can now never find anything the first try (l2_own_find, already
# unit-fallback-aware) didn't -- this fixture confirms the whole chain
# still resolves `x` correctly (not that l2_own_find_last specifically is
# what resolves it; see the -131 Part 2 report for that redundancy note).
int: x 5
size_t: want
fn: bump () size_t
    size_t: got
    got: sizeof: x
    return: got
end: bump
want: sizeof: int
size_t: got
got: bump()
if: got != want
    return: 90
return: 0
